# agent-context-layers — configuration
#
# Every script reads only these variables. Copy to `config.env` (git-ignored) or export
# them in your shell. Defaults point at the demo agent shipped in this repository.
#
# NOTE: AGENT_BACKUP_DIR must live OUTSIDE AGENT_SKILLS_ROOT. A backup inside the tree it
# protects gets picked up as content by every scanner that walks the tree.

# Directory holding the four context files (IDENTITY.md, USER.md, MEMORY.md, POINTERS.md).
# Default: <repo>/example-agent
# AGENT_HOME=/path/to/agent/home

# The skill tree. Default: $AGENT_HOME/skills
# AGENT_SKILLS_ROOT=/path/to/agent/home/skills

# Where backups, snapshots and archives go. Default: <repo>/.backups
# AGENT_BACKUP_DIR=/path/outside/the/tree

# How many context snapshots to keep. Default: 20
# AGENT_SNAPSHOT_KEEP=20

# How many backups to keep per source file in archive-baks.py. Default: 3
# AGENT_ARCHIVE_KEEP=3

# The four context files, in the order the checks walk them. Paths are relative to AGENT_HOME.
# AGENT_CONTEXT_FILES=IDENTITY.md USER.md MEMORY.md POINTERS.md

# Which of the four files must cross-reference the other three (mutual edges).
# Comma-separated file names; empty disables the check. Default: all four.
# AGENT_MUTUAL_FILES=IDENTITY.md,USER.md,MEMORY.md,POINTERS.md
